  "id": "apprehension",
  "term": "apprehension",
  "definition": "In historical psychology and philosophy, apprehension refers to a simple act of mind in which an object is directly grasped or brought before awareness. It can also mean the elementary awareness itself, or a simple belief or understanding, often contrasted with more complex thought such as judgment or comprehension.",
